},{"id":370471880,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE4ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:physics","name":"topic:physics","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1327318271,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzI3MzE4Mjcx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/crash","name":"crash","color":"885544","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/25","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25/labels","id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","number":25,"title":"4.8","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":351,"closed_issues":2337,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T15:17:38Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-06-20T19:44:12Z","updated_at":"2026-07-02T17:54:49Z","closed_at":"2026-07-02T17:54:14Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot 4.5 beta1\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10\n\n### Issue description\n\n`RuntimeNodeSelect` crashes on multiple places because it does not handle cases where a collision objects is not attached to a Node or Object. Which is the case for basically all PhysicsServer API created objects as they require no node or object to function.\n\nE.g.\n`RuntimeNodeSelect::_send_ids()` crashes on `SceneDebuggerObject obj(node->get_instance_id());`\n`RuntimeNodeSelect::_find_3d_items_at_rect()` crashes on an is_inside_tree() check.\n\nIn general assuming that any server RID object always has a Node or Object instance attached is faulty because all servers allow to work with server only created objects without any attached instance.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a server physics object that does not has a Node instance id attached to it and try to click its position with the RuntimeNodeSelect.\n\n```gdscript\nextends Node3D\n\nvar space : RID\nvar body : RID\nvar shape : RID\n\nfunc _ready():\n\tspace = get_world_3d().space\n\tbody = PhysicsServer3D.body_create()\n\tshape = PhysicsServer3D.box_shape_create()\n\tPhysicsServer3D.shape_set_data(shape, Vector3(100.0, 100.0, 100.0))\n\tPhysicsServer3D.body_add_shape(body, shape)\n\tPhysicsServer3D.body_set_space(body, space)\n\n\nfunc _exit_tree():\n\tPhysicsServer3D.free_rid(body)\n\tPhysicsServer3D.free_rid(shape)\n\n```\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nSee script examples, just drop it in a scene with a Camera3D and click somewhere with 3d input select to hit the server shape to make Godot crash.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"M